      "answerTypeCustomizations": {
        "documentation": "Also cover methods from the neighborhood module (e.g. can_move(), has_paint(), is_on_bucket(), is_on_paint(), take_paint(), turn_left()) using the same placeholder rules as built-ins.",
        "explainCode": "Only explain code the student has already written and run. Do not describe what ready_to_paint or needs_supplies should contain, or preview what either variable’s value will be before the student has written and tested it themselves.",
        "hint": "Do not state which function not should apply to in ready_to_paint or needs_supplies — deciding that is the point of the task. Point toward re-reading the instruction’s two clauses (e.g. “True if standing on a bucket, or True if out of paint”) rather than toward a specific line of code."
      }
    },
    "long_instructions": "# Write It: Restock at the Bucket\r\n\r\nYour Task: A painter walks down the street and needs paint. A paint bucket is somewhere along the way. At every square, check whether the Painter is standing on the bucket, and take the paint if it is.\r\n\r\nDo This:\r\n\r\n1. Run the program and watch the Painter. Does it end with any paint?\r\n2. After the first `move()`, write an `if` that checks whether the Painter is on the bucket. If it is, the Painter takes all the paint from the bucket. The bucket holds 3 units, and `take_paint()` takes 1 unit each time.\r\n3. Write the same kind of `if` after each of the other `move()` lines.\r\n4. Run your program. Which checks were True, and which were False?\r\n5. Use Validate to check your work.\r\n\r\nCoding Tip: An `if` has four parts: the `if` keyword, a condition, a colon, and an indented block.",
    "start_sources": {
      "files": {
        "0": {
          "id": "0",
          "name": "main.py",
          "contents": "from neighborhood import *\n\n# Painter setup: the Painter starts at the left end of the street, facing east.\n# Your code goes below.\n\n# Square 1\nmove()\n\n# Square 2\nmove()\n\n# Square 3\nmove()\n\n# Square 4\nmove()\n\n# Square 5\nmove()",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": true
        }
